{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":490806,"name":"Jean Pierre Soto Chirinos","username":"Jean_Pierre_Soto_Ch1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/a3d4f5/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T12:32:53.411Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi, I’m having an issue reconnecting to Grok Bot in Cursor.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe bot was working before, but now I’m unable to reconnect. I ran the Network Debugger / Check Access tool, and it shows that DNS resolution is working correctly, but most of the Cursor/Grok Bot services are failing.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe main error I can see is:\u003cbr\u003e\nAPI TLS: TLS certificate untrusted: SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter that, the API connection fails with ConnectError, and several other services return TypeError, including:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuth page\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuth UI\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuth service\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdates feed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdates download\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFeature flags\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOrigin API\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTelemetry\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVoice realtime\u003cbr\u003e\nThe debugger also shows the *.cursorvm.com computer endpoints as unavailable.\u003cbr\u003e\nI would like to reconnect Grok Bot, but I’m not sure whether the issue is caused by Cursor itself, my network configuration, a proxy/firewall, or a TLS certificate being injected somewhere in the connection.\u003cbr\u003e\nI have attached screenshots of the Network Debugger results.\u003cbr\u003e\nCould someone please help me identify what is causing the SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN error and what I need to configure or reset in order to reconnect Grok Bot?\u003cbr\u003e\nIf additional logs or diagnostic information are required, please let me know what I should provide.\u003cbr\u003e\nThanks in advance for your help.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot and try to use/reconnect to Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot fails to connect and remains unavailable.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the Network Debugger.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick Check Access to test the connection.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDNS resolution succeeds, but the API TLS check reports: TLS certificate untrusted: SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe API connection then fails with ConnectError.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMultiple related services also fail with TypeError, including authentication, updates, feature flags, Origin API, telemetry, and Voice Realtime.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe *.cursorvm.com computer endpoints are shown as unavailable.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRetry reconnecting to Grok Bot, but the issue persists.\u003cbr\u003e\nActual behavior:\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot cannot reconnect, and the Network Debugger reports TLS certificate and connection errors across multiple Cursor services.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot should connect normally and all required Cursor services should be reachable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/c/1/c1288d39a5f23f606464cc47321f84687bb53713.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/ryL247kVWDsZImt1wsFp6Zeb2Sf.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-14 072457.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/c/1/c1288d39a5f23f606464cc47321f84687bb53713.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-14 072457.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"ryL247kVWDsZImt1wsFp6Zeb2Sf\" width=\"398\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"363636\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-14 072457.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e595×746 14.6 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/4/d47e1797218f03e8d97334fd636373462bc48f50.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/ujNnfc02mxTStWnkUnMgf11sqNW.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-09-14 072451.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/d/4/d47e1797218f03e8d97334fd636373462bc48f50.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-14 072451.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"ujNnfc02mxTStWnkUnMgf11sqNW\" width=\"398\" height=\"500\" data-dominant-color=\"2D2D2D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-09-14 072451.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e601×755 28.3 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor grok bot 0.47.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003egrok 4.6\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-490806-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-490806-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-14T16:23:35.914Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":10.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171609,"topic_slug":"unable-to-reconnect-grok-bot-self-signed-cert-in-chain-and-multiple-connection-failures","display_username":"Jean Pierre Soto Chirinos","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":133734,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/unable-to-reconnect-grok-bot-self-signed-cert-in-chain-and-multiple-connection-failures/171609/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":490936,"name":"Jean Pierre Soto Chirinos","username":"Jean_Pierre_Soto_Ch1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/a3d4f5/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T14:52:53.038Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUpdate / resolved\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue was caused by \u003cstrong\u003eKaspersky HTTPS scanning\u003c/strong\u003e (SSL/TLS inspection), not by Grok Bot or my Cursor account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKaspersky intercepts HTTPS traffic and injects its own certificate into the chain. Network Debugger then reports:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eAPI TLS: TLS certificate untrusted: SELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter that, Auth, Updates, Feature flags, Origin API, Telemetry, Voice realtime, and \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e all failed. DNS still worked because it isn’t HTTPS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFix:\u003c/strong\u003e disable Kaspersky HTTPS/SSL scanning (or exclude Cursor / Grok Bot), or briefly use another network without that interception. After that, Grok Bot reconnects normally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHope this helps anyone hitting the same \u003ccode\u003eSELF_SIGNED_CERT_IN_CHAIN\u003c/code\u003e error.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-14T14:52:53.038Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":45.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171609,"topic_slug":"unable-to-reconnect-grok-bot-self-signed-cert-in-chain-and-multiple-connection-failures","display_username":"Jean Pierre Soto Chirinos","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[{"badges":[{"id":112,"name":"Checkpoint Restored","description":"Solved their own issue and came back to share","grant_count":367,"allow_title":false,"multiple_grant":true,"icon":"check","image_url":null,"listable":true,"enabled":true,"badge_grouping_id":6,"system":false,"slug":"checkpoint-restored","manually_grantable":true,"show_in_post_header":true,"badge_type_id":3}],"badge_types":[{"id":3,"name":"Bronze","sort_order":7}],"basic_user_badge":{"id":158350,"granted_at":"2026-09-14T16:23:35.498Z","grouping_position":0,"badge_id":112}}],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":133734,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/unable-to-reconnect-grok-bot-self-signed-cert-in-chain-and-multiple-connection-failures/171609/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_